             floating over a row of two text links along the bottom edge. The
             lockup is UNCHANGED — the same masthead device, the same tricolour
             rule, the same wish under it, at the same sizes R2l reverted them to
             — and what joins it is everything the end of the piece was already
             offering, gathered into the object that is offering it:

              · A THUMBNAIL of the card the reader can send. `send someone this
                card` asked them to download a picture they had never seen; the
                card they are being offered is the 1947 midnight they walked to,
                and showing it is the difference between a link and an offer.
                Its `src` is deliberately not in the markup — see the note on
                data-src below.
              · TWO ACTIONS, as real buttons in the piece's own quiet furniture
                register (10px tracked capitals, no rule, no box, no icon —
                exactly what the two text links were). `Share this card` is the
                Web Share API where the sheet can carry the FILE and the
                download everywhere else; `Start over` is the same restart it
                always was, and keeps its class so the stage's pointer
                exemptions and the engine's handler are untouched.
